00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.950 align:start position:0%
what are the council configurations to  make decisions in different policy areas  the Council meets in specialized  meetings known as council configurations  each configuration is made up of  ministers from the Member States it is  the ministers who vote on behalf of  their national government each  configuration deals with specific issues  for example economic and finance  ministers meet to discuss financial  affairs and ministers of justice discuss  justice issues in total the Council of  the EU meets in 10 different  configurations there is no hierarchy  among council configurations  however the General Affairs Council and  the Foreign Affairs Council have  specific roles defined in the EU  treaties meetings of each configuration  take place regularly some meet every  month some three to four times a year  and some on an ad-hoc basis over 150  preparatory bodies prepare the ground  for the meetings meetings are chaired by  the minister from the member state  holding the council presidency with the  exception of the Foreign Affairs Council  which is chaired by the High  Representative of the Union for Foreign  Affairs and security policy at their  meetings ministers work together to find  common solutions on issues of shared  interest the council takes decisions  using simple majority qualified majority  or unanimity voting when discussing or  voting on a legislative proposal council  meetings are public meetings are also  public when the council is debating  major issues affecting the interests of  the EU and its citizens find out all you  want to know about council  configurations and much more on  Concilium europa dot EU
 

